From ffb176d576f08cf89486f2096df125e0c76e600d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:00:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_offense_blowout_discount and
 v2_defense_blowout_discount_progressive

- v2_offense_blowout_discount (2026-09-28): discount a player's own team's 28+ point blowout games in his recency-weighted rate. Checked
  live against the case it was built for (C.J. Stroud's 6-20 loss, a 14-point margin) and measured exactly inert; the graded,
  sub-28-point script effect is reached by the shipped v2_offense_script_pool_blend.
- v2_defense_blowout_discount_progressive (2026-09-15): the same defense-side discount with quarter-checkpoint "decided" thresholds
  (21 at half, 17 after three, 24 final). The full 26-week confirm showed every scope's CI spanning 0, including START-RB: it washed
  out the real RB win along with the WR loss instead of separating them. The shipped v2_defense_blowout_discount keeps the
  final-margin test with a position gate.
Removes the own-team discount from _weighted_player_rates, OFFENSE_BLOWOUT_DISCOUNT_POSITIONS, the loaders' quarter-checkpoint
definition (PROGRESSIVE_BLOWOUT_CHECKPOINTS, _progressive_blowout_team_weeks) and its test. Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
